[SourceVersionDate "2022.06.19"]
[SourceQuality "1"]

{Position after 70.Nd5. "The most exciting game was that between Miss Price
and Mrs Bruce. Miss Price built up an almost overpowering attack which her
opponent only just managed to withstand; it took much coolness on her part and
after 70 moves the position [here] was reached. Black cannot win, because as
soon as a mating position is reached with the black pawn at h2 and K at h3 or
g3, the white knight has the freedom of the board and can roam with impunity,
for it cannot be captured because of stalemate. The draw came on the 82nd
move!" Source: BCM, Sept 1947, p281}  1/2-1/2

