{Adjournment position: RC Griffith writes, "Penrose should have played} 1. Kd3
Kc5 2. Ke4 Kb5 3. Kf5 Kc5 4. Kg4 Kb5 5. Bf6 Kb4 6. Bxh4 Be5 (6... Bxh4 7. Kxh4
{evidently loses}) 7. Kg5 Kxb3 8. Kf5 {, which wins. But he exchanged Bishops
before taking the K R P and so was a move behind, allowing Black to draw." 
[Annoyingly, Griffith doesn't give us the actual moves played! JS] Source: BCM,
June 1947, p180} 1/2-1/2

